WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.208
STEPHANIE WONG: This week,
we're talking about retail

00:00:02.208 --> 00:00:04.950
in the Cloud, Cloud
Run, and scaling SAP.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.050
I'm Stephanie, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.990
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:12.150
With 700 stores,
longtime retailer

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.880
Macy's has looked to Google
Cloud for data management

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.059
and analytics.

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:18.390
Google Cloud CEO
Thomas Kurian dives

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:20.790
into how GCP is
helping them streamline

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.170
operational functions.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:24.270
Check out the full article
to learn more about

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:27.070
how Google Cloud is helping
retails work faster,

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:28.920
smarter, and more securely.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:31.242
So you're excited about
the release of Node 12.

00:00:31.242 --> 00:00:32.700
And you just can't
wait for systems

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.380
to add new version support.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.300
Why not run it on
Google Cloud Run?

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.670
Using the function's framework
and a little bit of code,

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:41.760
Cloud Run can be set up
to easily deploy a Node 12

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:42.680
function.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.260
Breeze through this step-by-step
guide by Grant Timmerman.

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.840
Still searching for reasons to
start building on Cloud Run?

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:49.805
How about 12 more.

00:00:49.805 --> 00:00:51.180
Check out this
blog post to learn

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.370
exactly how Cloud Run
complies with each part

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.350
of the 12-factor
app methodology.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:56.500
It's simple.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.490
These factors act as a blueprint
to build applications that are

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.890
scalable, portable, and agile.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:04.110
Take a look to learn how
Cloud Run and the 12 factors

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:06.113
square up.

00:01:06.113 --> 00:01:07.530
You can see why
Cloud Run makes it

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.330
easy to scale serverless apps.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.430
But what about apps running
on virtual machines,

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:12.900
like SAP Server.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.480
Check out these best practices
for scaling SAP Server

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.350
on Google Cloud, and you'll
also get an in-depth comparison

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:22.620
of the two main approaches--
utilization-based auto scaling

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.420
and schedule-based scaling.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.128
Get ready for the
intelligent enterprise.

00:01:26.128 --> 00:01:28.212
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:28.212 --> 00:01:30.310
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:31.330
Have thoughts or ideas?

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:32.860
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.330
We'll see you in the Cloud.

